4 Adelie    Dream           56      3688.
Grouped mutate() and filter() compile aggregates and window functions to OVER (PARTITION BY ...). Window functions need an order, so call arrange() first or pass orderBy:.
A function given a PHP closure runs the query so far, loads the rows, and continues in memory, returning a DataFrame. Expressions with no faithful SQL translation do the same. They include round() (R rounds halves to even), first(), last(), nth(), iqr(), cumprod(), consecutive_id(), and median() or quantile() outside PostgreSQL.

show_query()
show_query(): Closure
The SQL a lazy table would run (database backends only).
Returns a function of a table, which returns the SQL string. Chain method: -&gt;showQuery(). Throws LogicException on invalid arguments. Example.


collect()
collect(): Closure
Run a lazy table’s query and return an in-memory Phibble.
Returns a function of a table, which returns a table. Chain method: -&gt;collect(). Example.

A first pipeline
Keep the penguins with a recorded body mass, summarize each species, and sort the species by average mass. The script reads penguins, size measurements for 344 penguins near Palmer Station, Antarctica, by URL.
composer require phpstats/phplyr

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


use Phibble\DataFrame;
use function Phplyr\{filter, group_by, summarize};
use function Phplyr\{arrange, desc, n, mean, sd};

$data = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phpstats'
    . '/datasets/main/csv';
$penguins = DataFrame::fromCsv("$data/penguins.csv");

echo $penguins |&gt;
    filter(fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;body_mass_g !== null) |&gt;
    group_by('species') |&gt;
    summarize(
        penguins: n(),
        avg_mass_g: mean('body_mass_g'),
        sd_mass_g: sd('body_mass_g'),
    ) |&gt;
    arrange(desc('avg_mass_g'));


use Phibble\DataFrame;
use function Phplyr\{phplyr, desc, n, mean, sd};

$data = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phpstats'
    . '/datasets/main/csv';
$penguins = DataFrame::fromCsv("$data/penguins.csv");

echo phplyr($penguins)
    -&gt;filter(fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;body_mass_g !== null)
    -&gt;groupBy('species')
    -&gt;summarize(
        penguins: n(),
        avg_mass_g: mean('body_mass_g'),
        sd_mass_g: sd('body_mass_g'),
    )
    -&gt;arrange(desc('avg_mass_g'));



