The ICC is the share of the variance left after the fixed effects that lies between subjects.
The intercept shifts are shrunk toward zero, so each is smaller than the subject’s average residual above.

Fuel economy by cylinders
mtcars has fuel consumption and design measurements for 32 cars from the 1974 Motor Trend magazine. mpg is miles per US gallon, hp is gross horsepower, and wt is weight in 1,000 lb.

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


// Fuel economy, power, and weight by number of cylinders,
// and each car's mpg against its cylinder group's mean.
$cars = DataFrame::fromCsv("$data/mtcars.csv") |&gt;
    rename(model: 'rownames');

echo $cars |&gt;
    group_by('cyl') |&gt;
    summarize(
        across(
            ['mpg', 'hp', 'wt'],
            ['mean' =&gt; mean(...), 'max' =&gt; max(...)],
        ),
        cars: n(),
    ) |&gt;
    mutate(across(
        where('double'),
        fn ($v) =&gt; round($v, 1),
    ));

$vsGroup = fn ($r, $g) =&gt; round(
    $r-&gt;mpg - mean('mpg')($g),
    1,
);
echo "\n\n", $cars |&gt;
    select('model', 'cyl', 'mpg') |&gt;
    mutate(vs_group: $vsGroup, _by: 'cyl') |&gt;
    arrange('cyl', desc('vs_group'));


// Fuel economy, power, and weight by number of cylinders,
// and each car's mpg against its cylinder group's mean.
$cars = phplyr(DataFrame::fromCsv("$data/mtcars.csv"))
    -&gt;rename(model: 'rownames')
    -&gt;get();

echo phplyr($cars)
    -&gt;groupBy('cyl')
    -&gt;summarize(
        across(
            ['mpg', 'hp', 'wt'],
            ['mean' =&gt; mean(...), 'max' =&gt; max(...)],
        ),
        cars: n(),
    )
    -&gt;mutate(across(
        where('double'),
        fn ($v) =&gt; round($v, 1),
    ));

$vsGroup = fn ($r, $g) =&gt; round(
    $r-&gt;mpg - mean('mpg')($g),
