mutate() adds or replaces columns. A value can be a row closure, a vector helper, a list with one value per row, a scalar, or null to drop the column. Later arguments see the columns made by earlier ones.

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


echo DataFrame::fromCsv("$data/penguins.csv") |&gt;
    drop_na() |&gt;
    select('species', 'bill_length_mm', 'bill_depth_mm', 'flipper_length_mm', 'body_mass_g') |&gt;
    mutate(
        bill_ratio: fn ($r) =&gt; round($r-&gt;bill_length_mm / $r-&gt;bill_depth_mm, 2),
        flipper: if_else(col('flipper_length_mm')-&gt;ge(200), 'long', 'short'),
        rank: min_rank(desc('body_mass_g')),
    ) |&gt;
    arrange('rank') |&gt;
    head(6);


